  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on comparing the variances of the two lotteries and preferring the one with the smaller variance. Lottery A offers 500 Euros with 100% probability, so its variance is 0. Lottery B offers 1000 Euros with 50% probability and 0 Euros with 50%, so its variance is calculated as: 0.5*(1000 - 500)^2 + 0.5*(0 - 500)^2 = 0.5*250000 + 0.5*250000 = 250000. Thus, Lottery A has a much smaller variance than Lottery B. The decision reason would therefore prefer Lottery A. The relevant information (variances) can be fully derived from the lotteries’ outcomes and probabilities, so the reason can be applied to this decision problem.",
